  "body": "### Summary\nAs a visitor without an account, I want the legacy sign-in prompts (a clear title, one line of explanation, an \"Ajouter un pseudo\" button), so that I understand why a list is empty and can sign in from there.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (validated legacy parity, ROADMAP). Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-11, side-by-side simulator captures 02, 06 (pseudos redacted, attached below when available).\n\n### Observed (2026-11-11, first launch, no account)\n- **Favoris**:\n  - Legacy: \"Connectez-vous pour accéder aux favoris\", \"Ajoutez un pseudo pour charger vos favoris et vos drapeaux.\", button \"Ajouter un pseudo\" (`HFRswift/Swift/Favorites.swift:600-612` @ `87fe0d1c`).\n  - SwiftHFR (@ `c04b89c9`, **to re-check on a current build**): \"Connexion requise\" then \"Aucun sujet que vous avez lu n'est connu\" (an empty-list text, wrong here) and \"Actualiser\" (useless without an account); title \"Drapeaux\".\n- **Topic list filter** (Favoris / Suivis / Lus):\n  - Legacy: icon, bold \"Connexion requise pour Favoris, Suivis et Lus\", subtitle \"Vous pouvez consulter \"Tous\" sans compte.\"\n  - SwiftHFR: the same words in one grey paragraph.\n\n### Scope\n- Favoris logged out: legacy title, text and \"Ajouter un pseudo\" button; no refresh.\n- Topic-list reminder: legacy hierarchy (icon, bold title, subtitle).\n- Favoris title and default view: \"Favoris\" as legacy, not \"Drapeaux\" (GAP-032; operator to confirm).\n- GAP-037 says \"same\": fix its wording through the PR's `### Ledger` section.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
